# VM Operations

## Primary hardware — **dp75k-mxl** (local D1–D3 + tape drive)

The workstation **dp75k-mxl** is the **physical host** for both the **model disks** and the **tape library** used in this repo’s LTFS workflows:

- **D1–D3:** mounted at **`/mnt/d1`**, **`/mnt/d2`**, **`/mnt/d3`** (ext4; UUID fstab via **`model-archival/scripts/install-archive-d123-fstab.sh`**). Verify with **`findmnt /mnt/d1`** etc.
- **LTO‑5 + LTFS:** **`/dev/sg1`**, **`/dev/nst0`** / **`/dev/st0`**; typical LTFS mount **`~/ltfs-mount`**. Tape scripts and plans live in **`/home/x/z/ai/ai-model-backup-tape/tape-archive/scripts/`** (e.g. **`ltfs-specialist-per-model-sequential-write.sh`**, **`specialist-tape-plan-split.py`**); run **`mkltfs`** and **`ltfs`** **on this machine** when operating the local tape drive.
- **Discovery caveat:** per‑model tape / plan scripts only queue revision directories that contain **`manifest.json`** (and a `main` or 40‑hex revision folder name). A **`/mnt/d1/specialist`** tree without those manifests will not appear in the plan until the archiver layout exists.

The SSH archival VM below (**`192.168.8.32`**) is a **different** machine (Ollama/D5, etc.) — **not** where this desk‑side tape drive is attached.

## Environment (archival VM — current)

- **SSH:** `ubuntu@192.168.8.32` (hostname **k80-ollama**). Set **`ARCHIVAL_VM=ubuntu@192.168.8.32`** for scripts; override anytime for another host.
- **OS:** Ubuntu (systemd). Use **`systemctl`** for services unless you know a unit is managed differently.
- **Project path:** use the model-archival checkout on that machine (historically **`/home/x/dev/model-archival/model-archival/`** on the old VM — resolve with `git -C ~ rev-parse --show-toplevel` on the new host).

**Legacy (retired Artix box):** `x@192.168.8.65` with mounts under **`/mnt/models/d1`** … **`/mnt/models/d5`**. Older docs and logs may still cite that layout; defaults in-repo now target **`.32`** and **`/mnt/models-d5`**.

## Disk layout (192.168.8.32)

| Label | Typical mount | Size (approx.) | Role |
|-------|---------------|----------------|------|
| D1 | `/mnt/models-d1` | 5.5 TB | Large models + scratch |
| D2 | `/mnt/models-d2` | 2.7 TB | Mid-size / overflow |
| D3 | `/mnt/models-d3` | 2.7 TB | GGUF / archiver infra |
| D5 | `/mnt/models-d5` | ~916 GB | D5-tier models, Ollama archive (`ollama/`), `~/z` snapshots (e.g. `z05012026/`) |

Paths use the **`/mnt/models-dN`** hyphenated prefix on this host (not **`/mnt/models/dN`**).

## dp75k-mxl — path cheat sheet (same host as tape)

| Disk | Mount point |
|------|-------------|
| models-d1 | `/mnt/d1` |
| models-d2 | `/mnt/d2` |
| models-d3 | `/mnt/d3` |

Automedia paths such as **`/media/x/models-d1`** may appear before fstab is installed; prefer **`/mnt/d*`** once configured.

Use these paths for **`verify-archive.py`**, **`par2_backfill_d2_d3.py`** (`--d1` / `--d2` / `--d3`), and **tape** scripts when working **on dp75k-mxl**. For SSH jobs targeting the archival VM, keep using **`/mnt/models-d*`** on **`.32`**. D5 may still follow the VM layout unless migrated.

**Ollama cache sync** (`model-archival/scripts/ollama-sync.sh`): default VM destination is **`/mnt/models-d5/ollama`**. Override with **`ARCHIVAL_VM_DEST`** or **`ARCHIVAL_VM_SITE_CYCLE`**. Sync is additive-only.

**Live Ollama + vLLM on D5:** defaults in **`ollama-hosting/config/env-archive-vm.sh`** and **`vllm-hosting/config/env-archive-vm-vllm.sh`** use **`/mnt/models-d5/ollama`** and **`/mnt/models-d5/vllm`**. Run **`deploy/consolidate-ollama-vllm-caches-to-d5.sh`** on the VM (dry-run first) if caches are still scattered on other disks.

## Before rebooting — always stop gracefully

From the model-archival repo on the VM:

```bash
bash ./stop.sh   # wait for "stopped cleanly"
# then reboot — skipping this can corrupt large disks (fsck recovery)
```

## If drives not mounted after reboot

Use your fstab / provisioning playbooks; there is no single shared `vm-mount-disks.sh` path guaranteed on **`.32`** — check **`deploy/vm-mount-disks.sh`** in-repo only if that script was installed for this host.

## If a drive shows "Structure needs cleaning"

```bash
sudo fsck.ext4 -y /dev/sdXN   # fix filesystem
sudo mount <mountpoint>       # then remount
```

## VPN (optional)

Some deployments route downloads through Surfshark/OpenVPN. If this host uses that stack, see historical notes in git history for **`openvpn-surfshark`** / **`.65`** Artix setup; otherwise use your standard VPN/docs for **`.32`**.

## Monitor downloads / archiver

```bash
watch -n 30 cat /mnt/models-d5/STATUS.md 2>/dev/null || true
```

## Local `~/.ssh/config`

If **`Host model-archival`** still points at **`192.168.8.65`**, update it to **`HostName 192.168.8.32`** and **`User ubuntu`** so muscle-memory matches the current box.
